<article class="env-lemma" id="0A7I">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0A7I">Lemma <span data-tag="0A7I">47.15.9</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be a surjective homomorphism of Noetherian rings. Let $\omega _ A^\bullet $ be a dualizing complex. Then $R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (B, \omega _ A^\bullet )$ is a dualizing complex for $B$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
